  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-06 driver_profile check was triggered by the material deviation on the trace, and the driver clears it: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 2, below the three-flag threshold, and 2 flags over driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 180 in the trailing window is a ratio of 0.011, far below the 0.05 test and above the 40-trip minimum that test requires. No repeat-deviation pattern is established. It follows that neither the FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) nor the driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) can be ordered on this record, and that the remedy cannot be resolved against the driver on profile evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02852"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-GEN-01 fixes exactly which profile counters may carry a finding, and for the POL-RD-06 test they are deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d and nothing else. The driver's lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags (4) is a deliberate near-synonym of the trailing-90-day figure and may not be substituted for it, just as rating 4.89, account_age_days 880, lifetime_trips 5346 and prior_no_show_flags 1 are context only. Any adverse finding built on those fields, including any suggestion that the driver is a serial long-hauler, must be discarded on the same footing as an uncited claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02852"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.prior_deviation_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's exposure is bounded by the POL-RD-02 arithmetic, not by the $20.66 headline in the claim. Stated on separate lines as the clause requires: charged_total is 20.66; recomputed_fare is ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 9.0 km optimal + 0.28 x 13.0 optimal minutes) x surge_multiplier 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-02852, and nowhere else) + 0.80 platform fee = 14.99; the refund is 5.67, rounded up to a payable 5.70. That is 27.4% of the charge, so the de minimis floor of 0.50 is passed but the 90% share that would convert a partial into a FULL_REFUND under POL-RD-02 is nowhere near, and the driver retains the base fare, the distance charge for the 9.0 optimal kilometres and the time charge for the 13.0 optimal minutes. The rider's characterisation of the whole fare as unjustified does not survive the clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02852", "EV-TRIP-02852"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is added on top of that distance refund. The fare_breakdown carries zero ERP lines and zero tolls, off_optimal_route_total is 0.00, erp_gantries is empty, and the airport surcharge is 0.0 on a trip that neither originates at nor ends at an airport, so there is no pass-through correction to be had under POL-RD-09(2) and no billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4). POL-RD-09(1) independently forbids any ERP figure being stacked onto the POL-RD-02 refund, so the rider's recovery is the single 5.70 figure and nothing more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02852", "EV-GPS-02852"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation, 'Road works', is on the record as the counterparty statement, and no artifact on the rider's side contradicts it; but the bundle holds no advisory to run it against. EV-ADVIS-02852-01 is MISSING, has no payload and carries weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the three-limb test in POL-RD-03 cannot be satisfied and the explanation can neither reduce the measured excess nor supply an amended optimal. I disclose that impairment expressly rather than presenting it as clean. Because the driver's statement names no advisory identifier, this is the POL-RD-13(1) gap in the bundle - an omission by the platform's third-party source - and not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact within POL-RD-10(5); the case should therefore be decided on the unimpaired trace as a monetary ruling rather than held open in escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02852-01", "EV-TRIP-02852"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: I find a route deviation on this trip and order a partial refund of SGD 5.70 to the rider. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02852, weight 1.0) is complete and unimpaired: 114 fixes, 10.0 s sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps. It measures 14.4 km against the booked optimal of 9.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02852, weight 1.0). That is an excess of 5.4 km, 60.0% of optimal, so both POL-RD-01 tests pass and the deviation is material. The fare is METERED. Using the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02852, weight 1.0) and its surge_multiplier of 1.0, charged_total is 20.66; recomputed_fare is (3.80 + 0.75 x 9.0 + 0.28 x 13.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 = 14.99; the refund is 20.66 - 14.99 = 5.67, rounded up to 5.70. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and 27.4% of charged_total, below the 90% full-refund share, so the ruling is PARTIAL_REFUND, not a full refund. The driver's explanation 'Road works' is an uncited traffic assertion. The only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02852-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), and no advisory ID is cited. Under POL-RD-13(1) this is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation, and under POL-RD-13(2) the excess stands at the measured figure. The driver's statement therefore reduces nothing. The material deviation triggered the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 2 and completed_trips_90d is 180; that is below the 3-flag threshold and the 0.05 ratio test (2/180 = 0.011), so no repeat-deviation pattern is established. There is no POL-RD-06(b) full-refund uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral. The chat log is empty, endpoints were not amended, and the trip is not pooled, so POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. No ERP, toll or surcharge correction is added under POL-RD-09: there are zero ERP lines and no airport surcharge. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07, so no corroboration is required. The monetary effect, SGD 5.70, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00 and will execute automatically on issue unless appealed under POL-GEN-04. Confidence is 0.95, capped at 1.0 by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts. The referee's discarded claim relying on prior_deviation_flags is not used."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-GEN-01 fixes exactly which profile counters may carry a finding, and for the POL-RD-06 test they are deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d and nothing else. The driver's lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags (4) is a deliberate near-synonym of the trailing-90-day figure and may not be substituted for it, just as rating 4.89, account_age_days 880, lifetime_trips 5346 and prior_no_show_flags 1 are context only. Any adverse finding built on those fields, including any suggestion that the driver is a serial long-hauler, must be discarded on the same footing as an uncited claim.",
