    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The GPS trace for TRP-02852 (EV-GPS-02852, weight 1.0) measures the trip at 14.4 km against the booked optimal of 9.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02852, weight 1.0) — an excess of 5.4 km, 60% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is established, and at over 50% it is material. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 114 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07(a)-(c) do not fire and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; the excess may rest on the trace alone. Nothing is excluded before the threshold: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02852) is empty, so POL-RD-04 has no rider instruction to read; no endpoint was amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null), so POL-RD-05 does not run; and the vehicle was RYDE_X, not a pooled trip, so POL-RD-12 does not apply and the 9.0 km booked optimal stands as the baseline.\n\nThe driver's explanation 'Road works' is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and there is none: EV-ADVIS-02852-01 is MISSING, has no payload, and carries weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Under POL-RD-13 that assertion is discarded, carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended optimal; because the driver's statement names no advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction, so the case is decided on the unimpaired trace and is not held open. The ruling records that the traffic assertion was discarded and that no advisory was on file.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, and the fare model is METERED. Stated on separate lines as the clause requires: charged_total = 20.66; recomputed_fare = (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 9.0 km + 0.28 x 13.0 min) x surge_multiplier 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-02852 and nowhere else, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP or toll, no fixed surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo discount = 14.99; refund = 20.66 - 14.99 = 5.67, rounded up to SGD 5.70 payable. That is above the 0.50 de minimis floor but only 27.4% of charged_total, far short of the 90% share that would convert it to a full refund, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 5.70. Nothing is added on top of that figure: erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.00, off_optimal_route_total is 0.00 and no airport or other fixed surcharge applies, so POL-RD-09 adds no pass-through correction under (2) and no billing-integrity refund under (4), and (1) forbids stacking ERP onto the POL-RD-02 amount.\n\nThe POL-RD-06 driver-profile check was run because the deviation is material: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 2 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 180 (ratio 0.011), below both the three-flag test and the 5%-at-40-trips test, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established. No POL-RD-06(b) uplift to a full refund is available to the rider and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the trailing-90-day figure the clause asks for and was not used.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts — the trace distance, the optimal distance and the fare figures — are carried by artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the missing advisory carries no deciding fact and does not lower it, which keeps confidence above the 0.70 floor and POL-RD-10(1) unengaged. The monetary effect of 5.70 is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of 8.00, so it executes automatically. This is a provisional ruling made without human review, and either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
